              0.718
            ]
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "In Chapter X unbounded operators on Hilbert space are examined. The distinction between symmetric and self-adjoint operators is carefully delineated and the Spectral Theorem for unbounded normal operators is obtained as a consequence of the bounded case. Stone's Theorem on one parameter unitary groups is proved and the role of the Fourier transform in relating differentiation and multiplication is exhibited."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "bbox": [
          0.125,
